---
/**
 * The mount point for the one approved React island.
 *
 * `client:only="react"` rather than `client:load`: the diagram is a drawing
 * whose only content is the interaction, and server-rendering it would ship a
 * second, static copy of ~40 SVG nodes into the HTML of a page that then
 * replaces them. Nothing here is content a search engine needs.
 *
 * What a search engine — and anyone with JavaScript off, or a slow build of it —
 * *does* need is the topology in words. That is the `<figcaption>` below, which
 * is not a fallback: it is always rendered, always visible, and says the same
 * thing the diagram says. The legacy page had no such text at all, and with
 * scripting unavailable it rendered a blank white page.
 *
 * The stylesheet is imported here, not inside the .tsx, so it is emitted as a
 * normal stylesheet on this page instead of arriving with the hydration bundle.
 */
import HelixDiagram from './HelixDiagram.tsx';
import './HelixDiagram.css';
---

<figure class="helix-figure">
  <HelixDiagram client:only="react" />

  <figcaption class="helix-figure__caption">
    <p>
      Diagrama de instalación técnica — Helix, EAC Montevideo 2025. Tres estaciones idénticas (A, B, C) dispuestas en
      triángulo alrededor de un router Wi-Fi central que también provee internet.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ethernet</strong> — el router alimenta las tres computadoras.</li>
      <li><strong>Wi-Fi</strong> — el router atiende a los móviles de las visitantes.</li>
      <li><strong>HDMI</strong> — cada computadora conduce su propia pantalla.</li>
      <li><strong>Datos NFC</strong> — cada estación tiene un lector NFC que reporta a su computadora.</li>
      <li><strong>Alimentación LED</strong> — cada computadora alimenta su tira LED.</li>
      <li><strong>Audio</strong> — la estación B envía audio al amplificador, y de ahí a tres pares de auriculares.</li>
    </ul>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /**
   * The page is a single 72ch measure, which is right for prose and wrong for a
   * 960-unit technical drawing: at the measure the station captions render
   * below the point where they can be read. The figure breaks out of the
   * measure up to the viewport, and only the figure does.
   */
  .helix-figure {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-6);
    width: min(64rem, 100vw - var(--s-12));
    align-self: center;
  }

  /* The words go back to the reading measure — only the drawing breaks out. */
  .helix-figure__caption {
    max-width: 72ch;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--t-small-size);
    line-height: var(--t-small-line);
  }

  .helix-figure__caption ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    padding-left: var(--s-4);
  }

  .helix-figure__caption strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: var(--t-body-weight);
  }
</style>
